1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,206
Why was Temu

2
00:00:01,206 --> 00:00:02,468
so cheap?

3
00:00:02,468 --> 00:00:03,439
Not just the

4
00:00:03,439 --> 00:00:05,520
factories or the ads.

5
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:06,526
The real trick

6
00:00:06,526 --> 00:00:08,000
was the parcel.

7
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,614
A US customs rule called

8
00:00:09,614 --> 00:00:10,920
de minimis let any

9
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,332
shipment under $800,

10
00:00:13,332 --> 00:00:14,880
sent to one person,

11
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:15,753
come in with

12
00:00:15,753 --> 00:00:16,790
no duties.

13
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:18,165
A store importing ten

14
00:00:18,165 --> 00:00:19,426
thousand phone cases

15
00:00:19,426 --> 00:00:20,642
in a container pays

16
00:00:20,642 --> 00:00:22,060
duty on all of them.

17
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:22,748
Ten thousand

18
00:00:22,748 --> 00:00:24,390
separate parcels?

19
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:25,440
No duty.

20
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:26,681
So every Temu

21
00:00:26,681 --> 00:00:28,170
order flew alone,

22
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:29,550
straight from China.

23
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:31,350
In fiscal 2024,

24
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:32,642
US customs handled

25
00:00:32,642 --> 00:00:35,850
1.36B of these parcels.

26
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:38,910
About 3.7M a day.

27
00:00:38,910 --> 00:00:40,686
Then the door closed:

28
00:00:40,686 --> 00:00:42,640
in May 2025 for China,

29
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,937
and in Aug. 2025

30
00:00:43,937 --> 00:00:45,320
for everyone.

31
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:47,276
So can Temu survive?

32
00:00:47,276 --> 00:00:48,213
Full story on

33
00:00:48,213 --> 00:00:49,280
